Build android sdcard image for raspberrypi5/raspberrypi4b.

   See https://raspberrytips.com/android-raspberry-pi-4/
   Here are the required steps to install Android on Raspberry Pi:
    
    Download the AOSP17 version for Raspberry Pi from Konstakang.
    Download Google Apps and save it on a USB memory stick.
    Flash the custom image to an SD card and start the Raspberry Pi.
    Reboot in recovery mode to install the Google Apps.

   Download from https://konstakang.com/devices/rpi5/AOSP17
   AOSP17-20261030-KonstaKANG-rpi5-ota.zip
   AOSP17-20261030-KonstaKANG-rpi5.zip
   unzip AOSP17-20261030-KonstaKANG-rpi5.zip

   Download from https://konstakang.com/devices/rpi4/AOSP17
   AOSP17-20261030-KonstaKANG-rpi4.zip
   AOSP17-20261030-KonstaKANG-rpi4-ota.zip
   unzip AOSP17-20261030-KonstaKANG-rpi4.zip

   Download Google Play Store:
   wget https://github.com/MindTheGapps/17.0.0-arm64/releases/download/MindTheGapps-17.0.0-arm64-20261022_132445/MindTheGapps-17.0.0-arm64-20261022_132445.zip

   Plugin usb3 stick to PC.
   sudo umount /dev/sda*
   (rpi5)  sudo dd if=~/Downloads/AOSP17-20261030-KonstaKANG-rpi5.img of=/dev/sda bs=4096 conv=notrunc,fsync status=progress
   (rpi4b) sudo dd if=~/Downloads/AOSP17-20261030-KonstaKANG-rpi4.img of=/dev/sda bs=4096 conv=notrunc,fsync status=progress
   sudo mount /dev/sda1 /mnt
   sudo vi /mnt/config.txt ( change from dtoverlay=android-sdcard to dtoverlay=android-usb, change to usb_max_current_enable=1 )  
   sync; sudo umount /mnt;
   Eject usb3 stick, plugin usb3 stick to rpi5/rpi4b.
   After setting up wifi and Timezone, turn on developer mode.
   Settings -> About tablet -> click build number 7 times
   Settings -> System -> Raspberry Pi settings -> ADB ( turn on ) 

   sudo dnf install adb
   cd ~/build-5sbc/android
   adb connect 192.168.86.20
   adb root
   adb shell
   du -h /system
   mount -o rw,remount /
   exit

   (rpi5)  adb push ~/Downloads/AOSP17-20261030-KonstaKANG-rpi5-ota.zip /sdcard
   (rpi4b) adb push ~/Downloads/AOSP17-20261030-KonstaKANG-rpi4-ota.zip /sdcard
   adb push ~/Downloads/MindTheGapps-17.0.0-arm64-20261022_132445.zip /sdcard

   Boot to TWRP recovery: Settings -> System -> Raspberry Pi settings -> Reboot to recovery -> F5 ( shutdown ) -> power on.
   (rpi5)  Install update -> Choose from internal storage -> AOSP17-20261030-KonstaKANG-rpi5-ota.zip -> Enter ->  Install update -> Choose from internal storage -> MindTheGapps-17.0.0-arm64-20261022_132445.zip -> Enter -> Reboot system
   (rpi4b) Install update -> Choose from internal storage -> AOSP17-20261030-KonstaKANG-rpi4-ota.zip -> Enter ->  Install update -> Choose from internal storage -> MindTheGapps-17.0.0-arm64-20261022_132445.zip -> Enter -> Reboot system

   Enable sound: Settings -> System -> Raspberry Pi settings -> Audio device (HDMI0).

   Open Google Play Store -> sign in. Install YouTube, Solitaire etc.

cd ~/build-5sbc/android
adb connect 192.168.86.20
adb root
adb shell
du -h /system
mount -o rw,remount /
exit

To install apks:
adb push drawing.apk /sdcard
adb push drawshape.apk /sdcard
adb push kaleidoscope.apk /sdcard
adb push myanalogclock.apk /sdcard
adb push randomsong.apk /sdcard
adb shell
cd /system/priv-app
ln -s /sdcard/drawing.apk .
ln -s /sdcard/drawshape.apk .
ln -s /sdcard/kaleidoscope.apk .
ln -s /sdcard/myanalogclock.apk .
ln -s /sdcard/randomsong.apk .
exit
adb install -r drawing.apk
adb install -r drawshape.apk
adb install -r kaleidoscope.apk
adb install -r myanalogclock.apk
adb install -r randomsong.apk
adb shell
mount -o ro,remount /
exit

To uninstall apks:
adb uninstall com.example.drawing
adb uninstall com.example.drawshape
adb uninstall com.example.kaleidoscope
adb uninstall com.example.myanalogclock
adb uninstall com.example.randomsong
